A||||10||Shaun41178||Fiero loses, then loses again||||8
Z||000000||Shaun41178||09-11-1999||04:55 AM||||I went to Norwalk tonight. Man there were a ton of good cars tonight. 2 Vipers showed up and tore the place up. One of them was red and one was blue. Both cars ran in the mid 12's. A 99 Vette went up against the blue Viper and pretty much got wasted like expected. The vette ran a mid 13 i believe.<BR>I also got to see the Buschar Racing Sponsored Eagle Talon run down the track. This car has been featured in Turbo mag several times and i about freaked when i saw it. Then he pulled into the staging lane next to mine and I about freaked again. We were right next to each otehr in the lanes and we chatted a bit. Well mostly I chatted and asked questions. has around 56 hp at the wheels and is running 27-30 psi of boost. He ran by himself and cranked off a 9.xxx e.t. Man it was sweet to see this car up close and in person.<P>So I happen to line up against a black 4th gen Firebird with an LT-1. I don't know what mods the car had if any but it was a manual tranny I think. So we pulled up to the line and I powerbrake a small spin to get the water off of my tires since i can't go around the water box cause there is no room to do so. So I get my tires clean and stage and the Bird does too. Green light and i get off teh line with a better R/T, my .821 to his 1.177. i hit a lazy 2.019 60' to his 2.080. So I am a little ahead about a 1/2 length to a length so I am happy at this point. Hit the 330' and I am still ahead although I can't tell by how much as he is not by my side but i am trying to keep looking strait ahead so he might have been just behind my window on my rear qtr panel or a bit further back. I run a 5.941 to his 5.948 to the 330'. Appraoching the 1/8 and i still don't see him next to me. I am still ahead by at least 3/4 car length. I run a 9.260 to his 9.266. We get to the 1000' and I see him next to me starting to pull a bit and then he took a car lenght right at the end real quick. He ended up running a 14.21 @ 101mph to my 14.66 @ 89 mph. Going 10 mph faster then me really made him pull fairly quickly after 1000' but I was a little upset that I almost won but didn't. I couldn't beleive I was ahead almost the whole race just to lose it in the last 300'. I was dissapointed but it gave me an idea of what some LT-1's run on the street and what I can expect from one from a role and one from a light. So it was a good learning experience for me.<P>Next race was against a 99 cobra convertible. I had plenty of cool down time and I have been hearing how the new cobras are slow and plus this was a convertible with a manual tranny so I thought that I had a really good chance of beating this thing. I then saw who was driving the car and it was an older man who looked like he was going through a midlife crisis so I had put it in my head that this guy didn't know how to drive this thing real good. Why I thought that I don't know. Call me arrogant cause I am young. So I do the powerbrake thing again to get the water off and I stage and so does the cobra. I powerbrake to get the revs up hoping that i take this guy out of the hole. Green light and this guy totally kicks my @ss off the line. His R/T is a .556 to my .803. Man I need to work on that don't I? But it didn't take long for me to get ahead of this guy, about a whole 60' to be exact. I run a 1.904 60' to his 2.138. By the 330' I have this guy by about a car to a car and a half. I run to 330' in 5.74 to his 6.043. I am getting pretty excited right now as I have a feeling that I am going to win. We get to the 1/8 and I run a 9.036 @ 74.2 mph to to his 9.187 @ 77 mph. I am about a half car length or so on this guy right now and it seems that every time he shifts he loses a bit of ground on me. We hit 1000' and he is next to me about a bumper ahead and i get this wrenching feeling in my stomach as i run a 11.929 to his 11.900. He begins to start pulling away and I know I can't catch up to him. He just has too much more top end then I do. He runs a 14.178 @ 99 mph to my 14.404 @ 90 mph. So close again but not enough top end. I need a different tranny with better gears to hold these other cars off in the top end. <BR>I guess I did give both drivers of the Cobra and the LT-1 a good scare though huh?  <BR>On a lighter note a did run a all new best at the track tonight. My best before is in my sig and here is my new best.<P>R/T:... .757<BR>60:... 1.873 OH YEA!!<BR>330... 5.692<BR>1/8... 8.960 OH YEA!!<BR>1/4.. 14.293 YEA YEA!! <P>This run came agaisnt a 12 second car. it could've helped if I ran this agasint the LT-1 or the Cobra. Oh well next time. The quest for lower e.t's is in full swing again.<BR>i did beat a Ford Tempo Twice. My only kills.||||reg||8
Z||000001||four50four||09-11-1999||10:01 AM||||Man that eagle must fly with the whopping 56 hp at the wheels. whats that, almost 100 at the crank  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000002||Patrick||09-11-1999||03:44 PM||||<BR>Shaun, I enjoy reading about your exploits at the strip, even though I'm probably another one of those "older" guys who's about to enter their mid-life crisis. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>You mention that you're thinking about changing your tranny to one with "better gears" that would allow you to hold off these other cars in the top end. I'm definitely no expert on these matters, but it would seem to me that there would have to be some kind of a trade off if you wished to gain better top end. Obviously, in this case it would be more of a sluggish bottom end. Since you haven't reported any problems with your car sitting there smoking it's tires at the starting line, I don't think giving up anything in the bottom end is going to gain you anything overall. It might even hurt your performance.<P>I know it's probably a tough pill to swallow, but it's more than possible that a <B>V6</B> in a Fiero is just NOT going to be able to handle a similarly modified <B>V8</B> in another car. You're simply at too much of a horsepower disadvantage. You may have to be satisfied that you have a nice looking, quick, relatively unique vehicle and leave it at that.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000003||theogre||09-11-1999||10:42 PM||||Fiero racing would be better in bracket than eliminator. These cars are pretty easy to get consistant performance out of.||||reg||3
Z||000004||fastonpumpgas||09-12-1999||01:21 AM||||What engine and mods did you do, I just want a ball parki, i am trying to build a 3.1 to smoke those 5.0s and Z28's out there?||||reg||5
Z||000005||Eric||09-12-1999||10:39 AM||||You'd be lucky just to hang with 5.0s and Z28s on a 3.1 rebuild.  I'm doing everything possible to build a high performance engine for my Fiero and still don't expect to run in the 14s.  Without forced induction or nitrous it is almost impossible to beat a Mustang or Camaro at the track.||||reg||9
Z||000006||Shaun41178||09-13-1999||03:46 AM||||Patrick: by me swapping gears(from a 3.06 to a 3.33) I will be losing top end in the car.  But that is ok by me cause there isn't anywhere around where I live where you can push your car safely over 100 mph without endangering someone else unless it is like 3 in the morning and no one is out and you want to see what your car can do.  I don't care about losing top end.  I would much rather have quicker acceleration.  Besides my top end is not that great anyway(120-125)<P>Mod for mod you are right a Fiero will not be able to hang with a V8.  However I am going after those stock V8's and the slightly modified ones.  I don't care if they are stock or not.  It is the fact that they have a V8 and I don't that makes me want to go out and do some damage.  Hell I almost beat two V8's at the track the other night with 70-100 more hp then me and that is if they are stock.  Unfortunately I lost in the last 300 feet in both of them.  In the 1/8 I would've beat both of them but their better gearing and more top end helped them to prevail.  Now if I raced both of these cars on the street i most likely would've desecrated both of them do to the fact that the street does not have VHT down to aid in traction plus the race would most likely not go up past 70 or so.<P>fastonpumpgas:  My mods include nitrous, underdrive pulley, crane ignition, coil and accel wires, and ported stock exhaust manifolds and that is it.  I run a 16.3 n/a and with nitrous I hit a best of 14.2 now.  not bad huh?<P>Eric: A properly built 3.1/3.2 can achieve 210+ hp and have great streetability and reliability as well.  My 2.8 is around 210-220 at the crank when on a 70 shot of nitrous.  With a 210 hp 3.1/3.2 it is possible to get 14 second timeslips especially if you have a manual tranny.  An auto can cut a 14 too but it will be a tad harder and will probably need a shift kit and 3.33 gearing(or not) to get there.  if not 14's then low 15's for sure.  Now that is hanging with a lot of 3rd gen birds and mustangs that are relatively stock.  Teh Fiero would be better for shorter bursts then the whole qtr mile. Remember the 3rd gen birds/camaros and late 80/early 90-mid 90 mustangs all had around 210-225 hp.  So if a Fiero has this much as well then it should run similar times that these cars ran.  But then you have to factor in the weight advantage of the Fiero.  about 3-500 pounds difference.  I would seem to me that a Fiero with 210 hp v6 should be able to handle a mustang and 3rd gen f-bodies with minor troubles.  Of course there will always be the few who have a good deal of mods in there cars to smoke you anytime.  Teh 4th gen f-bodies will be a littel tougher but could be possible to beat.  The new Ls-1's are pretty much top dogs and Fieros will probably need forced induction of some kind or a V8 to beat one of these.  But there are bad drivers out there as well so even without forced induction you still have a chance even if it is a remote one.  For example I saw a Lt-1 camaro Z28 turn a 14.5 at the track the other night.  <P>now add a Turbo or nitrous to your 3.1/3.2 then you can expect around 260+ hp depending on amount of boost or nitrous jetting.  With this setup you can expect high 4's to low 5's to 60 with this setup and low 13 second timeslips.  I plan on being in the low 13's next summer when I install my 3.2  Low 13's is what the new vettes run although I have yet to see a stock C5 break a 13.4 at the track.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||09-13-1999||08:25 AM||||Point #1:  For my money, any Fiero that runs th 1/4 in less than 15 sec is one badass Fiero.  Shaun, you da man.<P>Point #2:  I went out looking at new muscle cars last weekend.  My local Pontiac dealer had no Formula Firebirds, only Trans Ams.  Cheapest 6-speed:  $27,900.  The Ford dealer had some nice Mustang GT's (starting at $23,500) and Cobras ($29,000).  How much have you spent on your Fiero?  Again, you da man.||||reg||14
Z||000008||batboy||09-13-1999||11:38 AM||||Yeah! What Chadman said! There's an old saying: speed costs money, how fast do you want to go? I paid $1600 for my last Fiero and I like it better than any $16,000 new car I've seen lately.||||reg||6
Z||000009||Pretender||09-14-1999||03:21 AM||||I have also seen buscher run that yellow terd!, it is damn fast but he had to go with a chev. rear and tranny not to mention turning the engine sideways and elim. the awd(now rwd) to get into the 9's. Extreme motorsports is the best talon awd i've seen yet!, he ran like a 10.3 at englishtown the last time i was there. Eddie bello(9-sec RX-7) also has a bad ass rice burner!||||reg||10
Z||000010||Greg Piet||09-14-1999||05:01 AM||||Well looking back at the original post, against the pony, here is a bright side of the loss.  Taking reaction times out of the equation, the little fiero won by a couple of hundreths.  I think you said that the pony was a stick and you were running an automatic, so the win taking out reaction times doesnt fully negate the human factor.  But regardless, most excellent!  <BR>||||reg||1
